BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sphero Robotics
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260724T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260724T170000
UID:69b1b27819c54125aa032434@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an introduction to coding with Sphero robots. Sphe
 ro is a ball-shaped robot that can be programmed to “drive\,” “jump\
 ,” and change colours\, using block coding. For ages 6-12.\nRegistration
  is required. Parent/Caregiver must attend.\nInformation Collection Notice
 :\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publi
 c Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20
 (d). The information will only be used for event and program registration\
 , delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your in
 formation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 41
 6-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Spadina Road\, Children's Area
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b1b27819c54125aa032434
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Scratch Character Design for Kids (9+) PART 1
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260610T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260610T163000
UID:69fb7d0f177319280017db20@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This is Part 1 of a 2 PART program on Scratch Coding for Kid
 s. In Part 1 you will explore how to design your own customized sprites/ch
 aracters. The characters will be designed for a game that you code yourse
 lf in Scratch during Part 2. BE SURE TO SIGN UP FOR BOTH DAYS!\nThis class
  is open to children ages 9 and up. Computers will be provided.\nFor more 
 information about this program please contact dihonline@tpl.ca.
LOCATION:Jane/Sheppard\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fb7d0f177319280017db20
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
